# Everything here is excluded from the build context sent to the Docker daemon.
#
# Two reasons this matters more than it looks:
#
# 1. SECRETS. Both api/Dockerfile and web/Dockerfile do a broad `COPY api ./`
#    / `COPY web ./`. Without this file, a local .env sitting in either
#    directory gets baked into the image layer — and an image pushed to
#    Artifact Registry is readable by anyone with pull access, forever, even
#    if a later layer deletes the file.
#
# 2. SPEED. The context was including node_modules and .git, which on a repo
#    this size is most of the upload on every build.

.git
.gitignore
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build

# Secrets — never in an image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.production.example
*.pem
*.key

# Distribution archives
*.zip

# Runtime artifacts
status/status.json
status/directory.json
*.log
logs/
pgdata/
redisdata/

# Not needed at build time
*.md
!README.md
.github
# brand/ is NOT here on purpose. It was, and that silently broke the web image:
# web/Dockerfile copies it into the nginx root so the marketing site can serve
# /brand/icon.svg, and a path excluded from the build context makes COPY fail
# with "not found" — which reads like a missing directory rather than an
# ignored one. The two files have to agree; this is the reminder.
ops-console
docker-compose*.yml
setup.sh
**/__tests__
**/*.test.ts
.DS_Store
